<article class="article">
<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Pricing</span>
<h1>Honda Click vs Automatic Scooter: Hanoi Rental Cost Comparison</h1>
<p>The Honda Click rents at a verified 150,000 VND per day, 700,000 VND per week and 900,000 to 1,200,000 VND per month in Hanoi. The automatic scooter is not one machine but a category with two verified tiers, and the Click is the category's floor: the entry tier at 150,000 VND per day, shared with the Yamaha Mio, while the step-up tier of Honda Vision, Honda Air Blade and electric motorbike rents at 200,000 VND per day. This comparison reads the two price lists side by side honestly, including the part most riders miss, which is that the cheapest automatic scooter in the fleet is the Click itself.</p>
<p>We compare the daily, weekly and monthly structures at both tiers, the break-even logic each ladder produces, what the step-up premium actually buys as a ride, who each tier suits, and the deposit, gear and support questions that come with either choice. Start at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">Hanoi motorbike rental cost</a> hub, see the full model range at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> guide, and check common questions on the <a href="/faq/">rental FAQ</a>.</p>
<nav class="toc">
<ol>
<li><a href="#sec-1">The verified price ladders</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-2">Daily rate comparison</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-3">Weekly and monthly comparison</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-4">The break-even logic</a></li>
